WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:04.640
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and I had a chance
to see Maleficent this weekend so this is

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.650
going to be my review. In case you didn't
know, this is Disney using their giant spinning

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:13.209
wheel to create a new version of Sleeping
Beauty from the perspective of the evil witch,

00:00:13.209 --> 00:00:16.900
or at least the witch that was evil in the
classic Disney animated Sleepy Beauty movie.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.929
Since a lot of you might not have seen it
yet I'm going to do my non spoilery review

00:00:20.929 --> 00:00:25.519
first, then put this movie into context with
the classic animated movie and then during

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:28.609
the spoilery part I'll talk about my top 5
moments.

00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:33.920
If you're finding me for the first time, we
are thick in the middle of Summer movie season.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:37.649
I'm going to be doing weekly movie reviews.
So be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:42.780
Next up is Fault in Our Stars next Friday.
Feel free to leave me suggestions for movies

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.199
to review.

00:00:44.199 --> 00:00:49.559
So Maleficent is hopefully the first of a
new wave of Disney Villain movies. I love

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:51.719
movies about bad guys and girls. Maleficent
in my opinion, is like the Iron Man of Disney

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:56.090
Villains. She sits at the top. So naturally
it makes sense that she would get her own

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:00.550
movie first. I'll talk more about other Disney
villains I think need there own movies after

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:05.100
my review, but because this is a Villain movie
I want to spend most of this video talking

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.420
about the characters because that's why I
go see movies. The plot was fun and there

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.900
were a few surprises. But it's Angelina Jolie
and that Smile that really got me excited

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.210
to go see this.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:18.790
She was hypnotizing before Disney used all
that makeup and CG to make her mouth bigger.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:23.229
If you look at her in real life, yes. She
is famous for those lips. But the movie dials

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:28.400
that up to infinity. She can bite be with
those teeth anytime.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.280
It's pretty clear going into this that she's
going to be most people's favorite thing about

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:38.570
the movie. And she was definitely my favorite
thing. She fills that role with so much power

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:43.869
I'm starting to fantasize about her on Game
of Thrones as a brunette version of Cersei

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:47.920
Lannister. No offense to Lena Headey, you
are both amazing and I bow in submission.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.719
It's just a testament to Angelina that she
can play characters so well and be a leading

00:01:52.719 --> 00:01:56.719
lady. This is the weird thing about lead actors
in Hollywood. Usually lead characters are

00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:01.229
the most boring. Think about it this way.
Disney sells Pirates of The Caribbean movies

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:06.590
on Johnny Depp, not Jack Sparrow. At almost
every point in those movies, you're thinking

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:11.180
to yourself "look at Johnny Depp being amazing".

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:15.980
Character actors are way different. Like Michael
Sheen in Twilight or Tron Legacy. You're not

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.170
thinking about Michael Sheen when you watch
him. You're just thinking about Aro the Voltui

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.980
or Castor his Tron character.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.640
So sometimes, casting a big A List actor can
take you out of the story. I feel like Angelina

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.560
Jolie is such a great actress that she can
disappear into all of her roles. It makes

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:31.980
it so much more fun to watch all of her movies.
I'll talk more specifically about her Maleficent

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.670
character during spoilers.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:39.750
Elle Fanning on the other side of that equation
is quickly becoming one of my new favorite

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:44.340
young actors. Because Angelina Jolie drives
the whole movie, Sleeping Beauty is only a

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:49.550
supporting character. But she was still a
lot of fun to watch as a young princess who

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:56.550
doesn't even know what the word evil means
for most of the movie. Even though the movie

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:01.450
treats the classic Sleeping Beauty story in
this new complex way, all of the characters

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.440
except for Maleficent are pretty close to
what you remember from the original. Which

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.480
makes it a lot harder for them to stand out.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.650
I felt like she made an excellent foil for
Maleficent. She's not the primary antagonist

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.320
in the movie, but it's the interaction between
those two characters that really drives the

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.230
story forward and I totally loved it.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:24.970
This would be a great movie to take your Mom
to go see. Like it's a movie about the relationship

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:29.470
between mother's and daughters. The only thing
I didn't really like about the movie was the

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:34.320
voice over and the fact that the female characters
were still heavily defined by their relationships

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:40.760
with men in the film. Like they were defined
in terms of their romantic relationships.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:46.150
The voice over I understand. It's the Blade
Runner argument. In case you never heard about

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:50.260
it, there was this controversy with the movie
Blade Runner. One of the best science fiction

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:55.900
movies ever. When the movie was released the
studio wanted Ridley Scott to add a voice-over

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:59.820
to the movie because they felt like we, the
people watching it, were too dumb to follow

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:06.240
the story. Ridley Scott was forced to add
it and it really hurt the movie. There was

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.980
a directors cut way later that took the voice-over
out and it made the movie way better.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:16.989
This is all I could think about when the voice
over in Maleficent was happening. It's there

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:20.680
for little kids to help them follow the movie.
Because that's mostly who's going to go see

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:24.800
this movie. Little kids. So I understand why
they included it.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:30.450
I'll talk more about my issues with the female
characters during spoilers. So let's just

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:34.480
move into that. Careful for spoilers in case
you haven't seen the movie yet. But here are

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:38.890
my top 5 moments. Number 5 - Maleficent's
Use of Magic

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:43.440
Everything about magic in this movie is so
much more fun than OZ, the last big live action

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.050
Disney movie like this. In the movie Angelina
Jolie is the only one that gets to use magic

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:53.010
and it kind of seems like she's got crazy
power. That creates some story issues but

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:57.700
the visual way they presented magic, the special
effects, were great.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.920
Number 4 - The Three Fairy Godmothers

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:04.450
The movie twists the use of Fairy Godmother,
but I'm talking about the three fairies that

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:08.070
raise her. I loved the way they turned them
into the three stooges. It felt like they

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:12.700
made them way less nurturing than the original
cartoon versions. Like they were babysitters

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:18.110
just trying to earn a paycheck. I only recognized
Juno Temple, but she was in this movie called

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.880
The Brass Teapot, where she kept beating herself
up so that this magical teapot would spit

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.370
out money. That was super dark, but the fairies
smashing each other with stuff really made

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:27.020
me think of that. Like they were enjoying
beating the crap out of each other.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.800
It was totally hilarious and I loved the negative
spin on the characters. Like you would definitely

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:35.710
not want those three women to raise your child,
because they're terrible at it. Maleficent

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.320
was the real caretaker.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:41.050
Number 3 - The Big Differences from the Original
Cartoon

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:45.820
I'm talking about the metal vines inside the
castle, the dragon and making the King Sharto

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:49.420
Copley, the villain. There were a lot more
things they changed, but even if you haven't

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:54.490
seen the original cartoon in a long time the
things everyone remembers the most are Prince

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:58.150
Charming having to get through the vines at
the end and kill the dragon.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:04.580
Here's a big question though. If she could
turn Diaval into a Dragon at any time. Why

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:11.330
not just do it at the start and just destroy
the Castle and take back her wings. Why wait

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:17.190
16 years? It's just like the griffons in Lord
of The Rings. There wouldn't be a movie if

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.020
they did it the logical way.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.280
Number 2 - The Maleficent Aurora Relationship

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:26.100
This is the most important part of the movie,
the evolution of their relationship and how

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:31.900
it changes Maleficent. Somehow I don't think
she ever hated Aurora, even when she was a

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:36.410
baby. That's the whole idea, she was never
a villain in the true sense of the word. She

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:40.480
keeps saving her life and protecting her.
She even tried to undo the curse halfway through

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:41.460
the movie.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:46.030
If only we all had the magic to take back
shitty things we say. At least you can delete

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:46.800
awful tweets.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.980
and my Number 1 moment - This is really just
a specific moment in the film, but it's when

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:53.010
Maleficent takes Aurora into the Moors

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:58.740
That moment when Aurora starts to explode
with happiness and Maleficent just poof, shuts

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:02.830
her down. Like she's thinking 'oh my god,
that's enough of you." She just can't handle

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:04.240
all that pure emotion.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:08.230
I feel like if everyone could have a secret
power that would be it. Just be able to shut

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:12.169
people down like that when they get too crazy.
Poof, you sleep now.

00:07:12.169 --> 00:07:16.230
Now it's your turn though. Let me know what
your favorite part of the movie was!

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:21.430
Just to address my issue with the female characters.
I think the movie did a disservice to Maleficent

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:27.300
in particular just by making her so hung up
on Stefan. Yes he stole her wings. But she's

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:30.950
almost a god. So she could have just taken
them back at any time.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:36.250
The story forces her to wallow in misery at
the thought that everyone is awful and there's

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:40.340
no such thing as true love. In all fairness,
there was that long montage they just glossed

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:45.620
over, so I'm assuming that Stefan and Maleficent
were deeply in love and the movie just didn't

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.590
show that to us.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:52.980
Otherwise I think it was a great first entry
in a new line of big Disney Villain movies.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:58.620
The next one I think they should give a movie
to should be Ursula from Little Mermaid. Also,

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:02.620
if you haven't been watching it, Once Upon
A Time has been bringing a lot of the new

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:07.440
characters like Elsa from Frozen onto the
TV Show. They've already done Maleficent,

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:12.169
she was Pam from True Blood. But if you want
to see more alternative stories about Disney

00:08:12.169 --> 00:08:14.810
characters, that would be a good show to watch.

